"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe foreshadowing was well laid out for the twist.  \nThe protagonist distrusts and suspects everyone regarding a past incident.  \n\nIndeed, a person who knows a lot attracts a lot of suspicion and jealousy. Being a  is clearly not an easy job.  \n\nThe setting where the protagonist solves a case that the police missed in the past by herself is forced, but it seems unavoidable in this kind of novel. Let's just say the protagonist is smart.\n"